{"id":"U03","title":"Urban Sprouts","titleZh":"城市新芽","paras":[{"id":"U03-P1","sentences":[{"id":"U03-P1-S1","hard":false,"text":"Turning soil, pulling weeds, and harvesting cabbage sound like tough work for middle and high school kids."},{"id":"U03-P1-S2","hard":false,"text":"And at first it is, says Abby Jaramillo, who with another teacher started Urban Sprouts, a school garden program at four low-income schools."},{"id":"U03-P1-S3","hard":false,"text":"The program aims to help students develop science skills, environmental awareness, and healthy lifestyles."}],"zh":"翻土、拔草、收白菜，这些听起来对初中生和高中生来说都是苦活儿。艾比·哈拉米略说，起初确实如此。她和另一位老师在四所贫困学校创办了一个名为“城市新芽”的校园园艺项目。该项目旨在帮助学生培养科学技能、环保意识和健康的生活方式。"},{"id":"U03-P2","sentences":[{"id":"U03-P2-S1","hard":false,"text":"Jaramillo's students live in neighborhoods where fresh food and green space are not easy to find and fast food restaurants outnumber grocery stores."},{"id":"U03-P2-S2","hard":false,"text":"\"The kids literally come to school with bags of snacks and large bottles of soft drinks,\" she says."},{"id":"U03-P2-S3","hard":false,"text":"\"They come to us thinking vegetables are awful, dirt is awful, insects are awful.\""},{"id":"U03-P2-S4","hard":false,"text":"Though some are initially scared of the insects and turned off by the dirt, most are eager to try something new."}],"zh":"哈拉米略的学生住在很难买到新鲜食品、也少有绿地的社区里，那里的快餐店比杂货店还多。她说，这些孩子来上学时，手里拎着一袋袋零食和一大瓶大瓶的软饮料。他们来到我们这里时，觉得蔬菜很糟糕，泥土很糟糕，昆虫也很糟糕。尽管有些学生起初害怕虫子，也对泥土心生反感，但大多数人还是渴望尝试新事物。"},{"id":"U03-P3","sentences":[{"id":"U03-P3-S1","hard":false,"text":"Urban Sprouts' classes, at two middle schools and two high schools, include hands-on experiments such as soil testing, flower-and-seed dissection, tastings of fresh or dried produce, and work in the garden."},{"id":"U03-P3-S2","hard":false,"text":"Several times a year, students cook the vegetables they grow, and they occasionally make salads for their entire schools."}],"zh":"“城市新芽”的课程开设在两所初中和两所高中，内容包括动手实验，比如土壤检测、花卉和种子解剖、新鲜或干制农产品的品尝，还有在菜园里劳动。学生们每年有好几次烹调自己种出的蔬菜，偶尔还会为全校师生制作沙拉。"},{"id":"U03-P4","sentences":[{"id":"U03-P4-S1","hard":false,"text":"Program evaluations show that kids eat more vegetables as a result of the classes."},{"id":"U03-P4-S2","hard":false,"text":"\"We have students who say they went home and talked to their parents and now they're eating differently,\" Jaramillo says."}],"zh":"项目评估显示，上过这些课以后，孩子们吃的蔬菜变多了。哈拉米略说，有学生告诉我们，他们回家和父母谈了这件事，现在一家人的饮食方式都改变了。"},{"id":"U03-P5","sentences":[{"id":"U03-P5-S1","hard":false,"text":"She adds that the program's benefits go beyond nutrition."},{"id":"U03-P5-S2","hard":false,"text":"Some students get so interested in gardening that they bring home seeds to start their own vegetable gardens."},{"id":"U03-P5-S3","hard":true,"text":"Besides, working in the garden seems to have a calming effect on Jaramillo's special education students, many of whom have emotional control issues."},{"id":"U03-P5-S4","hard":false,"text":"\"They get outside,\" she says, \"and they feel successful.\""}],"zh":"她还说，这个项目的好处不仅仅在于营养。有些学生对园艺产生了浓厚的兴趣，甚至把种子带回家，自己开辟菜园。此外，在菜园里劳动似乎对哈拉米略所教的特殊教育学生有一种安抚作用，这些学生中有许多人存在情绪控制方面的问题。她说，他们走到户外，就会感到自己是成功的。"}],"words":[{"id":"U03-W01","lemma":"soil","surface":"soil","pos":"n.","zh":"土壤; 泥土","sent":"U03-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"turning soil","zh":"翻土"},{"en":"rich soil","zh":"肥沃的土壤"}]},{"id":"U03-W02","lemma":"pull","surface":"pulling","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 拉; 拔; 拖 n. 拉力; 拉扯","sent":"U03-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"pulling weeds","zh":"拔草"},{"en":"pull up","zh":"拔起; 停下"}]},{"id":"U03-W03","lemma":"harvest","surface":"harvesting","pos":"v. / n.","zh":"v. 收割; 收获 n. 收获; 收成","sent":"U03-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"harvesting cabbage","zh":"收白菜"},{"en":"a good harvest","zh":"丰收"}]},{"id":"U03-W04","lemma":"cabbage","surface":"cabbage","pos":"n.","zh":"卷心菜; 洋白菜","sent":"U03-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"grow cabbage","zh":"种白菜"}]},{"id":"U03-W05","lemma":"tough","surface":"tough","pos":"adj.","zh":"艰苦的; 困难的; 坚韧的","sent":"U03-P1-S1","phrases":[{"en":"tough work","zh":"苦活儿; 艰苦的工